<span class="ltx_bibblock">Beyond a gaussian denoiser: Residual learning of deep cnn for image denoising.

</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock"><span id="bib.bib63.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">IEEE transactions on image processing</span>, 26(7):3142–3155, 2017.

</span></li>
      
<li id="bib.bib64" class="ltx_bibitem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_role_refnum ltx_tag_bibitem">[64]</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock">
Bolei Zhou, Agata Lapedriza, Aditya Khosla, Aude Oliva, and Antonio Torralba.

</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock">Places: A 10 million image database for scene recognition.

</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock"><span id="bib.bib64.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">IEEE Transactions on Pattern Analysis and Machine Intelligence</span>, 2017.

</span></li>
      
<li id="bib.bib65" class="ltx_bibitem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_role_refnum ltx_tag_bibitem">[65]</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock">
Yuanzhi Zhu, Kai Zhang, Jingyun Liang, Jiezhang Cao, Bihan Wen, Radu Timofte, and Luc Van Gool.

</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock">Denoising diffusion models for plug-and-play image restoration.

</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock">In <span id="bib.bib65.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Proceedings of the IEEE/CVF Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition (CVPR) Workshops</span>, pages 1219–1229, June 2023.

</span></li>
    
</ul>
</section>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Technical Appendices</h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Settings for experiment in Figure <a href="#S1.F1" title="Figure 1 ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ NPN: Non-Linear Projections of the Null-Space for Imaging Inverse Problems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> </h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To illustrate this concept, we developed a toy example with <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}^{*}\in\mathbb{R}^{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}^{*}\in\mathbb{R}^{3}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{H}\in\mathbb{R}^{2\times 3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐇</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{H}\in\mathbb{R}^{2\times 3}</annotation></semantics></math>, and constructed an orthonormal vector <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{S}\in\mathbb{R}^{1\times 3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐒</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{S}\in\mathbb{R}^{1\times 3}</annotation></semantics></math> relative to the rows of <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐇</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{H}</annotation></semantics></math>, following Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ A.2 Algorithms for designing 𝐒 ‣ Appendix A Technical Appendices ‣ NPN: Non-Linear Projections of the Null-Space for Imaging Inverse Problems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>. A training dataset <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\mathbf{x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\mathbf{x})</annotation></semantics></math> was generated, consisting of random points within a circle centered at the origin. Using this dataset, we trained a two-layer neural network defined as <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{G}(\mathbf{Hx})=\mathbf{V}\phi(\mathbf{WHx})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐇𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝐕</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐖𝐇𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{G}(\mathbf{Hx})=\mathbf{V}\phi(\mathbf{WHx})</annotation></semantics></math>, with parameters <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{W}\in\mathbb{R}^{k\times 2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐖</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{W}\in\mathbb{R}^{k\times 2}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{V}\in\mathbb{R}^{1\times k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{V}\in\mathbb{R}^{1\times k}</annotation></semantics></math>, with <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=50" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>50</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=50</annotation></semantics></math> hidden neurons, optimized via the problem stated in (<a href="#S3.E3" title="In 3.2 Learning the NPN Prior ‣ 3 Method ‣ NPN: Non-Linear Projections of the Null-Space for Imaging Inverse Problems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>). For comparison, we also trained a network of similar size to directly reconstruct <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathbf{x}}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathbf{x}}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> from measurements <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Hx}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐇𝐱</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Hx}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Algorithms for designing <math id="A1.SS2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐒</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{S}</annotation></semantics></math></h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We developed an algorithm for obtaining <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐒</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{S}</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐇</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{H}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying that <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{S}\mathbf{H}^{\top}=\mathbf{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝐒𝐇</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>𝟎</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{S}\mathbf{H}^{\top}=\mathbf{0}</annotation></semantics></math>. The algorithm is based on the QR decomposition, first, computing a full QR decomposition of <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{H}^{\top}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝐇</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{H}^{\top}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times m}</annotation></semantics></math>, yielding an orthonormal basis <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Q}_{\text{full}}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐐</mi><mtext>full</mtext></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Q}_{\text{full}}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times n}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>. The columns from <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m+1</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Q}_{\text{full}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐐</mi><mtext>full</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Q}_{\text{full}}</annotation></semantics></math> form a basis for <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Null}(\mathbf{H})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Null</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐇</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Null}(\mathbf{H})</annotation></semantics></math>, which we denote by <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{N}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times(n-m)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐍</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{N}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times(n-m)}</annotation></semantics></math>. To construct a subspace of the null space, the algorithm samples a random Gaussian matrix <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{P}\in\mathbb{R}^{(n-m)\times p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐏</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{P}\in\mathbb{R}^{(n-m)\times p}</annotation></semantics></math>, which is orthonormalized via QR decomposition to produce <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{U}\in\mathbb{R}^{(n-m)\times p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐔</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{U}\in\mathbb{R}^{(n-m)\times p}</annotation></semantics></math>. This ensures that the resulting subspace is both diverse and well-conditioned. Finally, the matrix <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐒</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{S}</annotation></semantics></math> is obtained as <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{S}=\mathbf{U}^{\top}\mathbf{N}^{\top}\in\mathbb{R}^{p\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐒</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐔</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐍</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{S}=\mathbf{U}^{\top}\mathbf{N}^{\top}\in\mathbb{R}^{p\times n}</annotation></semantics></math>, which consists of <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> orthonormal vectors that span a random <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>-dimensional subspace within <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Null}(\mathbf{H})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Null</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐇</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Null}(\mathbf{H})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption" style="font-size:90%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span> <span id="alg1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Generate Orthonormal Rows to <math id="alg1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐇</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{H}</annotation></semantics></math> via QR decomposition</span></figcaption>
<div id="alg1.7" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">1:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Matrix </span><math id="alg1.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{H}\in\mathbb{R}^{m\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝐇</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">∈</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">ℝ</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">m</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{H}\in\mathbb{R}^{m\times n}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">, desired number of rows </span><math id="alg1.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.900em">p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l1.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">2:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l2.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Matrix </span><math id="alg1.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{S}\in\mathbb{R}^{p\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝐒</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">∈</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">ℝ</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">p</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{S}\in\mathbb{R}^{p\times n}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l2.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> whose rows are orthonormal and lie in </span><math id="alg1.l2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Null}(\mathbf{H})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">Null</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝐇</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Null}(\mathbf{H})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l2.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">3:</span></span>
              
              
            <math id="alg1.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Q}_{\mathrm{full}}\leftarrow\mathrm{QR}\bigl(\mathbf{H}^{\top}\bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝐐</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">full</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em" stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">QR</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝐇</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">⊤</mo></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Q}_{\mathrm{full}}\leftarrow\mathrm{QR}\bigl(\mathbf{H}^{\top}\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l3.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">4:</span></span>
              
              
            <math id="alg1.l4.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbf{N}\leftarrow\mathbf{Q}_{\mathrm{full}}[:,\,m+1\!:\!n]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝐍</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em" stretchy="false">←</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝐐</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">full</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">[</mo><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0em">:</mo><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">m</mi><mpadded style="width:0.628em;" width="0.628em"><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo></mpadded><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.128em">:</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">n</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{N}\leftarrow\mathbf{Q}_{\mathrm{full}}[:,\,m+1\!:\!n]</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l4.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><span id="alg1.l4.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;float:right;"><math id="alg1.l4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Nullspace basis, size <math id="alg1.l4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\times(n-m)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\times(n-m)</annotation></semantics></math>
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">5:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l5.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Sample </span><math id="alg1.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{P}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,I)\in\mathbb{R}^{(n-m)\times p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝐏</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">I</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">∈</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">ℝ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">n</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">m</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">p</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{P}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,I)\in\mathbb{R}^{(n-m)\times p}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l5.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">6:</span></span>
              
              
            <math id="alg1.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{U}\leftarrow\mathrm{QR}(\mathbf{P})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝐔</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em" stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">QR</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝐏</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{U}\leftarrow\mathrm{QR}(\mathbf{P})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l6.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><span id="alg1.l6.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;float:right;"><math id="alg1.l6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="alg1.l6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{U}\in\mathbb{R}^{(n-m)\times p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐔</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{U}\in\mathbb{R}^{(n-m)\times p}</annotation></semantics></math> with orthonormal columns
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l7.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">7:</span></span>
              
              
            <math id="alg1.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{S}\leftarrow\mathbf{U}^{\top}\,\mathbf{N}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝐒</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em" stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝐔</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝐍</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{S}\leftarrow\mathbf{U}^{\top}\,\mathbf{N}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l7.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><span id="alg1.l7.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;float:right;"><math id="alg1.l7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Resulting <math id="alg1.l7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\times n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\times n</annotation></semantics></math> matrix of orthonormal rows
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l8.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">8:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">return</span><span id="alg1.l8.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><math id="alg1.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝐒</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{S}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l8.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">
</span>
</div>
</div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.3 </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1 (PnP-NPN Convergence). ‣ 4 Theoretical analysis ‣ NPN: Non-Linear Projections of the Null-Space for Imaging Inverse Problems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></h3>

<div id="A1.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Here we provide the technical proof for Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1 (PnP-NPN Convergence). ‣ 4 Theoretical analysis ‣ NPN: Non-Linear Projections of the Null-Space for Imaging Inverse Problems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem1a" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem1a.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 1</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem1a.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(PnP-NPN Convergence)<span id="Thmtheorem1a.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem1a.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem1a.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem1a.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Consider the fidelity <math id="Thmtheorem1a.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(\tilde{\mathbf{x}})=\|\mathbf{H\tilde{x}-y}\|_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐇</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(\tilde{\mathbf{x}})=\|\mathbf{H\tilde{x}-y}\|_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, the denoiser <math id="Thmtheorem1a.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{\sigma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{\sigma}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies assumption <a href="#Thmassumption2" title="Assumption 2 (Bounded denoiser). ‣ 4 Theoretical analysis ‣ NPN: Non-Linear Projections of the Null-Space for Imaging Inverse Problems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, the matrix <math id="Thmtheorem1a.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐒</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{S}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies the RIP condition <a href="#Thmdefinition2" title="Definition 2 (Restricted Isometry Property ( ) ). ‣ 4 Theoretical analysis ‣ NPN: Non-Linear Projections of the Null-Space for Imaging Inverse Problems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> with constant <math id="Thmtheorem1a.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{\mathcal{M}_{D}}^{S}\in[0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mi>S</mi></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{\mathcal{M}_{D}}^{S}\in[0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>. The optimized network <math id="Thmtheorem1a.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies assumption <a href="#Thmdefinition3" title="Definition 3 (Convergence Improvement Zone (CIZ) by ϕ(𝐱^ℓ)). ‣ 4 Theoretical analysis ‣ NPN: Non-Linear Projections of the Null-Space for Imaging Inverse Problems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>. We run iterations as in (<a href="#S4.E4" title="In 4 Theoretical analysis ‣ NPN: Non-Linear Projections of the Null-Space for Imaging Inverse Problems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>) in the convergence improvement zone for <math id="Thmtheorem1a.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell=1,\dots,L_{\phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell=1,\dots,L_{\phi}</annotation></semantics></math>. The algorithm converges to a fixed point if</span></p>
<table id="A1.E9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho\triangleq(1+\delta)\left(\left\|\mathbf{I}-\alpha(\mathbf{H}^{\top}\mathbf{H}+\mathbf{S}^{\top}\mathbf{S})\right\|+(1+\Delta_{\mathcal{M_{D}}}^{S})\|\mathbf{S}\|\right)&lt;1" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>≜</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐈</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝐇</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐇</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐒</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐒</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></msub><mi>S</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐒</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho\triangleq(1+\delta)\left(\left\|\mathbf{I}-\alpha(\mathbf{H}^{\top}\mathbf{H}+\mathbf{S}^{\top}\mathbf{S})\right\|+(1+\Delta_{\mathcal{M_{D}}}^{S})\|\mathbf{S}\|\right)&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem1a.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem1a.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem1a.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Proof:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|\mathbf{x}^{\ell+1}-\mathbf{x}^{*}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|\mathbf{x}^{\ell+1}-\mathbf{x}^{*}\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\|\mathrm{T}(\mathbf{x}^{\ell})-\mathrm{T}(\mathbf{x}^{*})\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\|\mathrm{T}(\mathbf{x}^{\ell})-\mathrm{T}(\mathbf{x}^{*})\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\overset{\text{Assumption \ref{def:den}}}{\leq}(1+\delta)\left\|\mathbf{x}^{\ell}-\alpha\left(\mathbf{H}^{\top}(\mathbf{H}\mathbf{x}^{\ell}-\mathbf{y})+\mathbf{S}^{\top}(\mathbf{S}\mathbf{x}^{\ell}-(\mathbf{Sx}^{*}+\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{Hx}^{*}))\right)-\mathbf{x}^{*}\right\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic" mathsize="0.700em">Assumption </mtext><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic" mathsize="0.700em"><a href="#Thmassumption2" title="Assumption 2 (Bounded denoiser). ‣ 4 Theoretical analysis ‣ NPN: Non-Linear Projections of the Null-Space for Imaging Inverse Problems" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a></mtext></mrow></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>𝐇</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐇𝐱</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>𝐒</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐒𝐱</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐒𝐱</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐇𝐱</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\overset{\text{Assumption \ref{def:den}}}{\leq}(1+\delta)\left\|\mathbf{x}^{\ell}-\alpha\left(\mathbf{H}^{\top}(\mathbf{H}\mathbf{x}^{\ell}-\mathbf{y})+\mathbf{S}^{\top}(\mathbf{S}\mathbf{x}^{\ell}-(\mathbf{Sx}^{*}+\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{Hx}^{*}))\right)-\mathbf{x}^{*}\right\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(1+\delta)\left\|\mathbf{x}^{\ell}-\mathbf{x}^{*}-\alpha(\mathbf{H}^{\top}\mathbf{H}+\mathbf{S}^{\top}\mathbf{S})(\mathbf{x}^{\ell}-\mathbf{x}^{*})+\mathbf{S}^{\top}\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{Hx}^{*})\right\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝐇</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐇</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐒</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐒</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐒</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐇𝐱</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(1+\delta)\left\|\mathbf{x}^{\ell}-\mathbf{x}^{*}-\alpha(\mathbf{H}^{\top}\mathbf{H}+\mathbf{S}^{\top}\mathbf{S})(\mathbf{x}^{\ell}-\mathbf{x}^{*})+\mathbf{S}^{\top}\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{Hx}^{*})\right\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(1+\delta)\left\|(\mathbf{I}-\alpha(\mathbf{H}^{\top}\mathbf{H}+\mathbf{S}^{\top}\mathbf{S}))(\mathbf{x}^{\ell}-\mathbf{x}^{*})+\mathbf{S}^{\top}\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{Hx}^{*})\right\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐈</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝐇</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐇</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐒</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐒</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐒</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐇𝐱</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(1+\delta)\left\|(\mathbf{I}-\alpha(\mathbf{H}^{\top}\mathbf{H}+\mathbf{S}^{\top}\mathbf{S}))(\mathbf{x}^{\ell}-\mathbf{x}^{*})+\mathbf{S}^{\top}\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{Hx}^{*})\right\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\overset{\text{triang. ineq.}}{\leq}(1+\delta)\left\|\mathbf{I}-\alpha(\mathbf{H}^{\top}\mathbf{H}+\mathbf{S}^{\top}\mathbf{S})\right\|\|\mathbf{x}^{\ell}-\mathbf{x}^{*}\|+(1+\delta)\|\mathbf{S}^{\top}\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{Hx}^{*})\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>≤</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic" mathsize="0.700em">triang. ineq.</mtext></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐈</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝐇</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐇</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐒</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐒</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐒</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐇𝐱</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\overset{\text{triang. ineq.}}{\leq}(1+\delta)\left\|\mathbf{I}-\alpha(\mathbf{H}^{\top}\mathbf{H}+\mathbf{S}^{\top}\mathbf{S})\right\|\|\mathbf{x}^{\ell}-\mathbf{x}^{*}\|+(1+\delta)\|\mathbf{S}^{\top}\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{Hx}^{*})\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\overset{\text{Definition \ref{def:error}}}{\leq}(1+\delta)\left\|\mathbf{I}-\alpha(\mathbf{H}^{\top}\mathbf{H}+\mathbf{S}^{\top}\mathbf{S})\right\|\|\mathbf{x}^{\ell}-\mathbf{x}^{*}\|+(1+\delta)\|\mathbf{S}\|\|\mathbf{S}\left(\tilde{\mathbf{x}}^{\ell}-\mathbf{x}_{*}\right)\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic" mathsize="0.700em">Definition </mtext><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic" mathsize="0.700em"><a href="#Thmdefinition3" title="Definition 3 (Convergence Improvement Zone (CIZ) by ϕ(𝐱^ℓ)). ‣ 4 Theoretical analysis ‣ NPN: Non-Linear Projections of the Null-Space for Imaging Inverse Problems" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a></mtext></mrow></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐈</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝐇</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐇</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐒</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐒</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐒</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐒</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\overset{\text{Definition \ref{def:error}}}{\leq}(1+\delta)\left\|\mathbf{I}-\alpha(\mathbf{H}^{\top}\mathbf{H}+\mathbf{S}^{\top}\mathbf{S})\right\|\|\mathbf{x}^{\ell}-\mathbf{x}^{*}\|+(1+\delta)\|\mathbf{S}\|\|\mathbf{S}\left(\tilde{\mathbf{x}}^{\ell}-\mathbf{x}_{*}\right)\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\overset{\text{Definition \ref{def:rip}}}{\leq}(1+\delta)\left(\left\|\mathbf{I}-\alpha(\mathbf{H}^{\top}\mathbf{H}+\mathbf{S}^{\top}\mathbf{S})\right\|+(1+\Delta_{\mathcal{M}_{D}}^{S})\|\mathbf{S}\|\right)\|\mathbf{x}^{\ell}-\mathbf{x}^{*}\|\qed{}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic" mathsize="0.700em">Definition </mtext><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic" mathsize="0.700em"><a href="#Thmdefinition2" title="Definition 2 (Restricted Isometry Property ( ) ). ‣ 4 Theoretical analysis ‣ NPN: Non-Linear Projections of the Null-Space for Imaging Inverse Problems" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a></mtext></mrow></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐈</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝐇</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐇</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐒</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐒</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mi>S</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐒</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_italic" lspace="0em" mathvariant="italic" separator="true">∎</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\overset{\text{Definition \ref{def:rip}}}{\leq}(1+\delta)\left(\left\|\mathbf{I}-\alpha(\mathbf{H}^{\top}\mathbf{H}+\mathbf{S}^{\top}\mathbf{S})\right\|+(1+\Delta_{\mathcal{M}_{D}}^{S})\|\mathbf{S}\|\right)\|\mathbf{x}^{\ell}-\mathbf{x}^{*}\|\qed{}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.4 </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2 (Convergence of NPN Regularization). ‣ 4 Theoretical analysis ‣ NPN: Non-Linear Projections of the Null-Space for Imaging Inverse Problems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a></h3>

<div id="Thmtheorem2a" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem2a.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 2</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem2a.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Convergence of NPN Regularization)<span id="Thmtheorem2a.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem2a.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem2a.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem2a.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Consider the iterations of the PnP-NPN algorithm defined in (<a href="#S4.E4" title="In 4 Theoretical analysis ‣ NPN: Non-Linear Projections of the Null-Space for Imaging Inverse Problems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>) for <math id="Thmtheorem2a.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell=1,\dots,L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell=1,\dots,L</annotation></semantics></math>. Assume that the estimation error of the trained network <math id="Thmtheorem2a.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{G}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">G</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{G}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 1 (Prior mismatch). ‣ 4 Theoretical analysis ‣ NPN: Non-Linear Projections of the Null-Space for Imaging Inverse Problems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, and that both <math id="Thmtheorem2a.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐒</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{S}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem2a.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐇</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{H}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfy the Restricted Isometry Property (RIP) over the manifold <math id="Thmtheorem2a.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{D}</annotation></semantics></math> with constants <math id="Thmtheorem2a.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{\mathcal{M}_{D}}^{S},\Delta_{\mathcal{M}_{D}}^{H}\in[0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mi>S</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mi>H</mi></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{\mathcal{M}_{D}}^{S},\Delta_{\mathcal{M}_{D}}^{H}\in[0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>. Further assume that the residual term <math id="Thmtheorem2a.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{N}(\mathbf{H}\mathbf{x}^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐇𝐱</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{N}(\mathbf{H}\mathbf{x}^{*})</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="Thmtheorem2a.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz continuous, thus <math id="Thmtheorem2a.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathrm{N}(\mathbf{Hx}^{*})\|\leq K(1+\Delta_{M_{D}}^{H})\|\mathbf{x^{*}}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐇𝐱</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mi>H</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathrm{N}(\mathbf{Hx}^{*})\|\leq K(1+\Delta_{M_{D}}^{H})\|\mathbf{x^{*}}\|</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, after <math id="Thmtheorem2a.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math> iterations, the NPN regularization term satisfies the following upper bound:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathrm{G}(\mathbf{y})-\mathbf{S\tilde{x}}^{\ell+1}\|\leq C_{1}\|\mathbf{x}^{*}-\mathbf{x}^{\ell}\|+K\|\mathbf{x}^{*}\|(1+\Delta_{\mathcal{M}_{D}}^{H})+C_{2}\|\mathbf{x}^{\ell}-\mathbf{x}^{\ell+1}\|," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝐒</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mi>H</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathrm{G}(\mathbf{y})-\mathbf{S\tilde{x}}^{\ell+1}\|\leq C_{1}\|\mathbf{x}^{*}-\mathbf{x}^{\ell}\|+K\|\mathbf{x}^{*}\|(1+\Delta_{\mathcal{M}_{D}}^{H})+C_{2}\|\mathbf{x}^{\ell}-\mathbf{x}^{\ell+1}\|,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem2a.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem2a.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where
<math id="Thmtheorem2a.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{1}=\left(\frac{1}{2\alpha}+(1+\Delta_{\mathcal{M}_{D}}^{S})^{2}+K(1+\Delta_{\mathcal{M}_{D}}^{H})(1+\Delta_{\mathcal{M}_{D}}^{S})\|\mathbf{x}^{*}\|\right),\quad C_{2}=\left((1+\Delta_{\mathcal{M}_{D}}^{S})+\frac{1}{\sqrt{2\alpha}}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mi>S</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mi>H</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mi>S</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mi>S</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{1}=\left(\frac{1}{2\alpha}+(1+\Delta_{\mathcal{M}_{D}}^{S})^{2}+K(1+\Delta_{\mathcal{M}_{D}}^{H})(1+\Delta_{\mathcal{M}_{D}}^{S})\|\mathbf{x}^{*}\|\right),\quad C_{2}=\left((1+\Delta_{\mathcal{M}_{D}}^{S})+\frac{1}{\sqrt{2\alpha}}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Proof:</span> We begin by recalling the definition of the regularization function:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi(\mathbf{x})=\|\mathbf{S}\mathbf{x}-\mathbf{S}\mathbf{x}^{*}-\mathrm{N}(\mathbf{H}\mathbf{x}^{*})\|." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐒𝐱</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝐒𝐱</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐇𝐱</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi(\mathbf{x})=\|\mathbf{S}\mathbf{x}-\mathbf{S}\mathbf{x}^{*}-\mathrm{N}(\mathbf{H}\mathbf{x}^{*})\|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">From the iteration difference, we have:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\phi(\mathbf{x}^{\ell+1})-\phi(\mathbf{x}^{\ell})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\phi(\mathbf{x}^{\ell+1})-\phi(\mathbf{x}^{\ell})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\|\mathbf{S}(\mathbf{x}^{\ell+1}-\mathbf{x}^{\ell})\|^{2}+2\langle\mathbf{x}^{\ell+1}-\mathbf{x}^{\ell},\mathbf{S}^{\top}(\mathbf{S}\mathbf{x}^{\ell}-\mathbf{S}\mathbf{x}^{*}-\mathrm{N}(\mathbf{H}\mathbf{x}^{*}))\rangle." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐒</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐒</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐒𝐱</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝐒𝐱</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐇𝐱</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\|\mathbf{S}(\mathbf{x}^{\ell+1}-\mathbf{x}^{\ell})\|^{2}+2\langle\mathbf{x}^{\ell+1}-\mathbf{x}^{\ell},\mathbf{S}^{\top}(\mathbf{S}\mathbf{x}^{\ell}-\mathbf{S}\mathbf{x}^{*}-\mathrm{N}(\mathbf{H}\mathbf{x}^{*}))\rangle.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Define the intermediate step:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{q}^{\ell}=\mathbf{x}^{\ell}-\alpha\,\mathbf{S}^{\top}(\mathbf{S}\mathbf{x}^{\ell}-\mathbf{S}\mathbf{x}^{*}-\mathrm{N}(\mathbf{H}\mathbf{x}^{*})),\quad\alpha&gt;0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝐪</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐒</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐒𝐱</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝐒𝐱</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐇𝐱</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{q}^{\ell}=\mathbf{x}^{\ell}-\alpha\,\mathbf{S}^{\top}(\mathbf{S}\mathbf{x}^{\ell}-\mathbf{S}\mathbf{x}^{*}-\mathrm{N}(\mathbf{H}\mathbf{x}^{*})),\quad\alpha&gt;0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Optimality implies:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathbf{x}^{\ell+1}-\mathbf{q}^{\ell}\|\leq\|\mathbf{x}^{*}-\mathbf{q}^{\ell}\|." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝐪</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝐪</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathbf{x}^{\ell+1}-\mathbf{q}^{\ell}\|\leq\|\mathbf{x}^{*}-\mathbf{q}^{\ell}\|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Substituting the definition of <math id="A1.SS4.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{q}^{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐪</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{q}^{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> and rearranging gives:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|\mathbf{x}^{\ell+1}-\mathbf{x}^{\ell}+\alpha\,\mathbf{S}^{\top}(\mathbf{S}\mathbf{x}^{\ell}-\mathbf{S}\mathbf{x}^{*}-\mathrm{N}(\mathbf{H}\mathbf{x}^{*}))\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐒</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐒𝐱</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝐒𝐱</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐇𝐱</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|\mathbf{x}^{\ell+1}-\mathbf{x}^{\ell}+\alpha\,\mathbf{S}^{\top}(\mathbf{S}\mathbf{x}^{\ell}-\mathbf{S}\mathbf{x}^{*}-\mathrm{N}(\mathbf{H}\mathbf{x}^{*}))\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\|\mathbf{x}^{*}-\mathbf{x}^{\ell}+\alpha\,\mathbf{S}^{\top}(\mathbf{S}\mathbf{x}^{\ell}-\mathbf{S}\mathbf{x}^{*}-\mathrm{N}(\mathbf{H}\mathbf{x}^{*}))\|^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐒</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐒𝐱</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝐒𝐱</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐇𝐱</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\|\mathbf{x}^{*}-\mathbf{x}^{\ell}+\alpha\,\mathbf{S}^{\top}(\mathbf{S}\mathbf{x}^{\ell}-\mathbf{S}\mathbf{x}^{*}-\mathrm{N}(\mathbf{H}\mathbf{x}^{*}))\|^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Expanding both sides and reorganizing terms, we obtain:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 2\alpha\langle\mathbf{x}^{\ell+1}-\mathbf{x}^{\ell},\mathbf{S}^{\top}(\mathbf{S}\mathbf{x}^{\ell}-\mathbf{S}\mathbf{x}^{*}-\mathrm{N}(\mathbf{H}\mathbf{x}^{*}))\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐒</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐒𝐱</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝐒𝐱</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐇𝐱</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 2\alpha\langle\mathbf{x}^{\ell+1}-\mathbf{x}^{\ell},\mathbf{S}^{\top}(\mathbf{S}\mathbf{x}^{\ell}-\mathbf{S}\mathbf{x}^{*}-\mathrm{N}(\mathbf{H}\mathbf{x}^{*}))\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\|\mathbf{x}^{*}-\mathbf{x}^{\ell}\|^{2}-\|\mathbf{x}^{\ell+1}-\mathbf{x}^{\ell}\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\|\mathbf{x}^{*}-\mathbf{x}^{\ell}\|^{2}-\|\mathbf{x}^{\ell+1}-\mathbf{x}^{\ell}\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad+2\alpha\langle\mathbf{x}^{*}-\mathbf{x}^{\ell},\mathbf{S}^{\top}(\mathbf{S}\mathbf{x}^{\ell}-\mathbf{S}\mathbf{x}^{*}-\mathrm{N}(\mathbf{H}\mathbf{x}^{*}))\rangle." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐒</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐒𝐱</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝐒𝐱</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐇𝐱</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad+2\alpha\langle\mathbf{x}^{*}-\mathbf{x}^{\ell},\mathbf{S}^{\top}(\mathbf{S}\mathbf{x}^{\ell}-\mathbf{S}\mathbf{x}^{*}-\mathrm{N}(\mathbf{H}\mathbf{x}^{*}))\rangle.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p7.1" class="ltx_p">Dividing by <math id="A1.SS4.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> and substituting back into (<a href="#A1.E11" title="In A.4 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix A Technical Appendices ‣ NPN: Non-Linear Projections of the Null-Space for Imaging Inverse Problems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>) yields:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\phi(\mathbf{x}^{\ell+1})-\phi(\mathbf{x}^{\ell})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\phi(\mathbf{x}^{\ell+1})-\phi(\mathbf{x}^{\ell})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\|\mathbf{S}(\mathbf{x}^{\ell+1}-\mathbf{x}^{\ell})\|^{2}+\frac{1}{2\alpha}\|\mathbf{x}^{*}-\mathbf{x}^{\ell}\|^{2}-\frac{1}{2\alpha}\|\mathbf{x}^{\ell+1}-\mathbf{x}^{\ell}\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐒</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\|\mathbf{S}(\mathbf{x}^{\ell+1}-\mathbf{x}^{\ell})\|^{2}+\frac{1}{2\alpha}\|\mathbf{x}^{*}-\mathbf{x}^{\ell}\|^{2}-\frac{1}{2\alpha}\|\mathbf{x}^{\ell+1}-\mathbf{x}^{\ell}\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad+\langle\mathbf{x}^{*}-\mathbf{x}^{\ell},\mathbf{S}^{\top}(\mathbf{S}\mathbf{x}^{\ell}-\mathbf{S}\mathbf{x}^{*}-\mathrm{N}(\mathbf{H}\mathbf{x}^{*}))\rangle." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐒</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐒𝐱</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝐒𝐱</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐇𝐱</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad+\langle\mathbf{x}^{*}-\mathbf{x}^{\ell},\mathbf{S}^{\top}(\mathbf{S}\mathbf{x}^{\ell}-\mathbf{S}\mathbf{x}^{*}-\mathrm{N}(\mathbf{H}\mathbf{x}^{*}))\rangle.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p8.1" class="ltx_p">Next, applying Assumptions <a href="#Thmdefinition2" title="Definition 2 (Restricted Isometry Property ( ) ). ‣ 4 Theoretical analysis ‣ NPN: Non-Linear Projections of the Null-Space for Imaging Inverse Problems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> and <a href="#Thmdefinition3" title="Definition 3 (Convergence Improvement Zone (CIZ) by ϕ(𝐱^ℓ)). ‣ 4 Theoretical analysis ‣ NPN: Non-Linear Projections of the Null-Space for Imaging Inverse Problems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, we bound:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\langle\mathbf{x}^{*}-\mathbf{x}^{\ell},\mathbf{S}^{\top}(\mathbf{S}\mathbf{x}^{\ell}-\mathbf{S}\mathbf{x}^{*}-\mathrm{N}(\mathbf{H}\mathbf{x}^{*}))\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐒</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐒𝐱</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝐒𝐱</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐇𝐱</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\langle\mathbf{x}^{*}-\mathbf{x}^{\ell},\mathbf{S}^{\top}(\mathbf{S}\mathbf{x}^{\ell}-\mathbf{S}\mathbf{x}^{*}-\mathrm{N}(\mathbf{H}\mathbf{x}^{*}))\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad\leq\|\mathbf{S}(\mathbf{x}^{\ell}-\mathbf{x}^{*})\|^{2}+K(1+\Delta_{\mathcal{M}_{D}}^{H})(1+\Delta_{\mathcal{M}_{D}}^{S})\|\mathbf{x}^{*}\|\|\mathbf{x}^{\ell}-\mathbf{x}^{*}\|." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="1.278em">≤</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐒</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mi>H</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mi>S</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad\leq\|\mathbf{S}(\mathbf{x}^{\ell}-\mathbf{x}^{*})\|^{2}+K(1+\Delta_{\mathcal{M}_{D}}^{H})(1+\Delta_{\mathcal{M}_{D}}^{S})\|\mathbf{x}^{*}\|\|\mathbf{x}^{\ell}-\mathbf{x}^{*}\|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p9.1" class="ltx_p">Substituting this back into (<a href="#A1.Ex17" title="In A.4 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix A Technical Appendices ‣ NPN: Non-Linear Projections of the Null-Space for Imaging Inverse Problems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a>), we get:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\phi(\mathbf{x}^{\ell+1})-\phi(\mathbf{x}^{\ell})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\phi(\mathbf{x}^{\ell+1})-\phi(\mathbf{x}^{\ell})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex20.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\|\mathbf{S}(\mathbf{x}^{\ell+1}-\mathbf{x}^{\ell})\|^{2}-\frac{1}{2\alpha}\|\mathbf{x}^{\ell+1}-\mathbf{x}^{\ell}\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐒</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\|\mathbf{S}(\mathbf{x}^{\ell+1}-\mathbf{x}^{\ell})\|^{2}-\frac{1}{2\alpha}\|\mathbf{x}^{\ell+1}-\mathbf{x}^{\ell}\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad+\frac{1}{2\alpha}\|\mathbf{x}^{*}-\mathbf{x}^{\ell}\|^{2}+\|\mathbf{S}(\mathbf{x}^{\ell}-\mathbf{x}^{*})\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐒</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad+\frac{1}{2\alpha}\|\mathbf{x}^{*}-\mathbf{x}^{\ell}\|^{2}+\|\mathbf{S}(\mathbf{x}^{\ell}-\mathbf{x}^{*})\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad+K(1+\Delta_{\mathcal{M}_{D}}^{H})(1+\Delta_{\mathcal{M}_{D}}^{S})\|\mathbf{x}^{*}\|\|\mathbf{x}^{\ell}-\mathbf{x}^{*}\|." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mi>H</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mi>S</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad+K(1+\Delta_{\mathcal{M}_{D}}^{H})(1+\Delta_{\mathcal{M}_{D}}^{S})\|\mathbf{x}^{*}\|\|\mathbf{x}^{\ell}-\mathbf{x}^{*}\|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p10.1" class="ltx_p">Using the triangle inequality and the RIP property again, we simplify:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi(\mathbf{x}^{\ell})\leq(1+\Delta_{\mathcal{M}_{D}}^{S})\|\mathbf{x}^{\ell}-\mathbf{x}^{*}\|+K(1+\Delta_{\mathcal{M}_{D}}^{H})\|\mathbf{x}^{*}\|." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mi>S</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mi>H</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi(\mathbf{x}^{\ell})\leq(1+\Delta_{\mathcal{M}_{D}}^{S})\|\mathbf{x}^{\ell}-\mathbf{x}^{*}\|+K(1+\Delta_{\mathcal{M}_{D}}^{H})\|\mathbf{x}^{*}\|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p11.1" class="ltx_p">Hence, regrouping terms, we achieve a final compact form analogous to the desired inequality:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|\mathrm{G}(\mathbf{y})-\mathbf{S}\mathbf{x}^{\ell+1}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝐒𝐱</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|\mathrm{G}(\mathbf{y})-\mathbf{S}\mathbf{x}^{\ell+1}\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex23.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\phi(\mathbf{x}^{\ell+1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\phi(\mathbf{x}^{\ell+1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\left(\frac{1}{2\alpha}+(1+\Delta_{\mathcal{M}_{D}}^{S})^{2}+K(1+\Delta_{\mathcal{M}_{D}}^{H})(1+\Delta_{\mathcal{M}_{D}}^{S})\|\mathbf{x}^{*}\|\right)\|\mathbf{x}^{*}-\mathbf{x}^{\ell}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mi>S</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mi>H</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mi>S</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\left(\frac{1}{2\alpha}+(1+\Delta_{\mathcal{M}_{D}}^{S})^{2}+K(1+\Delta_{\mathcal{M}_{D}}^{H})(1+\Delta_{\mathcal{M}_{D}}^{S})\|\mathbf{x}^{*}\|\right)\|\mathbf{x}^{*}-\mathbf{x}^{\ell}\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad+K(1+\Delta_{\mathcal{M}_{D}}^{H})\|\mathbf{x}^{*}\|+\left((1+\Delta_{\mathcal{M}_{D}}^{S})+\frac{1}{\sqrt{2\alpha}}\right)\|\mathbf{x}^{\ell+1}-\mathbf{x}^{\ell}\|.\qed{}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mi>H</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mi>S</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">.</mo><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_italic" lspace="0.0835em" mathvariant="italic" separator="true">∎</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad+K(1+\Delta_{\mathcal{M}_{D}}^{H})\|\mathbf{x}^{*}\|+\left((1+\Delta_{\mathcal{M}_{D}}^{S})+\frac{1}{\sqrt{2\alpha}}\right)\|\mathbf{x}^{\ell+1}-\mathbf{x}^{\ell}\|.\qed{}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.5 </span>Neural network details</h3>

<div id="A1.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">SPC</span>: For the single-pixel camera experiments, we employ a ConvNeXt-inspired backbone <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">33</a>]</cite>. The network has five ConvNeXt blocks, each comprising two successive <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3\times 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3\times 3</annotation></semantics></math> convolutions with ReLU activations. A final <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3\times 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3\times 3</annotation></semantics></math> convolutional layer projects the 128 features back to one channel. The output feature map is flattened and passed through a linear module to match the measurement dimensionality. We use cosine-based positional encoding with a dimension of 256, and set the number of blocks to 5 and the base channel width to 128.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS5.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS5.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">MRI and Deblurring</span>: To train <math id="A1.SS5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{G}</annotation></semantics></math> for the MRI and Deblurring experiments, we use a U-Net architecture <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib42" title="" class="ltx_ref">42</a>]</cite> with three downscaling and three upscaling modules. Each module consists of two consecutive Conv → ReLU blocks. The downscaling path uses max pooling for spatial reduction, starting with 128 filters and increasing up to 1,024 at the bottleneck. The upscaling path performs nearest-neighbor interpolation before each module, progressively reducing the number of filters. A final 2D convolutional layer without activation produces the output. Skip connections link corresponding layers in the encoder and decoder.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.6 </span>Plug and Play algorithms</h3>

<div id="A1.SS6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This work uses the PnP-FISTA, its unrolled version, and RED-FISTA algorithms to validate the proposed approach. Below is shown algorithms for PnP and RED formulation and their NPN-regularized counterparts. For unrolling FISTA, the only change is that the denoiser <math id="A1.SS6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{D}_{\sigma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{D}_{\sigma}</annotation></semantics></math> is changed to a trainable deep neural network that is optimized in an end-to-end manner.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg2" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_minipage ltx_align_middle ltx_framed ltx_framed_top" style="width:138.0pt;">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption" style="font-size:80%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg2.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 2</span> </span> PnP-FISTA</figcaption>
<div id="alg2.6" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg2.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">1:</span></span>
              
              
            <math id="alg2.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L,\mathbf{H},\mathbf{y},\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">L</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">𝐇</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">𝐲</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">α</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L,\mathbf{H},\mathbf{y},\alpha</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg2.l1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
