<figure id="A1.F6" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.01608v1/gamma_deblurring.svg" id="A1.F6.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:286/216;" width="286" height="216"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 6: </span>Effect of <math id="A1.F6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> on PSNR (dB) in deblurring reconstruction, with <math id="A1.F6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=0.5\times 10^{-4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>0.5</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=0.5\times 10^{-4}</annotation></semantics></math>. The maximum PSNR of 31.25 dB is achieved when <math id="A1.F6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma=0.263" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.263</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma=0.263</annotation></semantics></math>.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A1.F7" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.01608v1/gamma_curve.svg" id="A1.F7.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:286/216;" width="286" height="216"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 7: </span>Effect of <math id="A1.F7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> in NPN on PSNR (dB) for MRI reconstruction, with <math id="A1.F7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=1\times 10^{-4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=1\times 10^{-4}</annotation></semantics></math>. The maximum PSNR of 33.67 dB is achieved when <math id="A1.F7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma=6\times 10^{-3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma=6\times 10^{-3}</annotation></semantics></math>.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A1.F8" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.01608v1/CS_gamma_curve.svg" id="A1.F8.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:286/212;" width="286" height="212"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 8: </span>Effect of <math id="A1.F8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> on PSNR (dB) in SPC reconstruction, with <math id="A1.F8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=8\times 10^{-4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=8\times 10^{-4}</annotation></semantics></math>. The maximum PSNR of 21.17 dB is achieved when <math id="A1.F8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma=1.04" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1.04</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma=1.04</annotation></semantics></math>.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A1.F9" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.01608v1/SPC_convergence_crS.png" id="A1.F9.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/283;" width="476" height="283" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 9: </span>Effect of the low-dimensional subspace dimension <math id="A1.F9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p/n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p/n</annotation></semantics></math> and projection matrix <math id="A1.F9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐒</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{S}</annotation></semantics></math> design on signal convergence in SPC reconstruction, with <math id="A1.F9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=8\times 10^{-4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=8\times 10^{-4}</annotation></semantics></math>.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A1.SS11.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS11.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Additionally, we implemented several state-of-the-art denoisers into the PnP framework. We also change the FISTA algorithm used in the paper to an alternating direction method of multipliers (ADMM) formulation. This algorithm splits the optimization problem into two subproblems: the data fidelity and the prior. We employed several state-of-the-art denoisers such as Restormer
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib60" title="" class="ltx_ref">60</a>]</cite>, DnCNN <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib63" title="" class="ltx_ref">63</a>]</cite>, DnCNN-Lipschitz <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib43" title="" class="ltx_ref">43</a>]</cite>, and DRUNet <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib62" title="" class="ltx_ref">62</a>]</cite>. We validated the image deblurring application with a Gaussian kernel bandwidth <math id="A1.SS11.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma=2.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma=2.0</annotation></semantics></math>. We used 200 iterations of the PnP-ADMM algorithm, the step size <math id="A1.SS11.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=0.5</annotation></semantics></math>, and the value of <math id="A1.SS11.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma=0.7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.7</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma=0.7</annotation></semantics></math>. In Table 1 are shown the obtained results. Here, the proposed regularization function consistently improves the baseline PnP-ADMM algorithm.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.T7" class="ltx_table">
<div id="A1.T7.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:241.5pt;height:24.9pt;vertical-align:-10.8pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-59.4pt,6.1pt) scale(0.670363940564802,0.670363940564802) ;">
