<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 7: </span>Comparison of PnP-ADMM method for image deblurring with <math id="A1.T7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma=2.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma=2.0</annotation></semantics></math> using different denoisers. The best result is highlighted in <span id="A1.T7.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-bg-color:#BFDFDF;">bold teal</span>, and the second-best in <span id="A1.T7.6" class="ltx_text ltx_underline" style="--ltx-bg-color:#FFDFBF;">orange underline</span>.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS12" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.12 </span>Analysis on the selction of <math id="A1.SS12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> and data adaptation</h3>

<div id="A1.SS12.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS12.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The selection of the size of <math id="A1.SS12.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐒</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{S}</annotation></semantics></math> is important for the optimization (<a href="#S3.E3" title="In 3.2 Learning the NPN Prior ‣ 3 Method ‣ NPN: Non-Linear Projections of the Null-Space for Imaging Inverse Problems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>) as the bigger value of <math id="A1.SS12.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>, the more challenging the projection estimation becomes. We show the estimation error in the following table, showing that the error increases by increasing the number of rows of <math id="A1.SS12.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐒</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{S}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.T8" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 8: </span>Projection error for different values of <math id="A1.T8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p/n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p/n</annotation></semantics></math>.</figcaption>
<table id="A1.T8.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="A1.T8.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T8.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_tt"><math id="A1.T8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p/n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒑</mi><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold">/</mo><mi>𝒏</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p/n</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A1.T8.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt"><math id="A1.T8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\|\mathbf{Sx}^{*}-\mathrm{G}(\mathbf{y})\|}{\|\mathbf{Sx}^{*}\|}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mrow><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold" stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐒𝐱</mi><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold">∗</mo></msup><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold">−</mo><mrow><mi>𝐆</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold" stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold" stretchy="false">‖</mo><msup><mi>𝐒𝐱</mi><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold">∗</mo></msup><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold" stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\|\mathbf{Sx}^{*}-\mathrm{G}(\mathbf{y})\|}{\|\mathbf{Sx}^{*}\|}</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T8.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T8.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">0.1</td>
<td id="A1.T8.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">0.1031</td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T8.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T8.2.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r">0.3</td>
<td id="A1.T8.2.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">0.1544</td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T8.2.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T8.2.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r">0.5</td>
<td id="A1.T8.2.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">0.1821</td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T8.2.5" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T8.2.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r">0.7</td>
<td id="A1.T8.2.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">0.2566</td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T8.2.6" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T8.2.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb ltx_border_r">0.9</td>
<td id="A1.T8.2.6.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">0.2305</td></tr>
</table>
</figure>
<div id="A1.SS12.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS12.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Additionally, to illustrate the effect of the data-driven adaptability of <math id="A1.SS12.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐒</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{S}</annotation></semantics></math>, we clarify the following. In compressed sensing, to span the null-space, we design a matrix orthogonal to <math id="A1.SS12.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐇</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{H}</annotation></semantics></math> via the QR decomposition, and via optimization using the regularization in Eq. (<a href="#S3.E3" title="In 3.2 Learning the NPN Prior ‣ 3 Method ‣ NPN: Non-Linear Projections of the Null-Space for Imaging Inverse Problems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>), which promotes that the rows of <math id="A1.SS12.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐒</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{S}</annotation></semantics></math> lie in the null-space of <math id="A1.SS12.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐇</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{H}</annotation></semantics></math>. To analyze how the data distribution affects the design of <math id="A1.SS12.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐒</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{S}</annotation></semantics></math>, we optimize four matrices, one for each dataset (MNIST, FashionMNIST, CIFAR10, and CelebA), cross-validating the data-driven invertibility loss <math id="A1.SS12.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{x}}\|\mathbf{x}-\mathbf{S}^{\dagger}\mathbf{S}\mathbf{x}\|_{2}^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐒</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐒𝐱</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{x}}\|\mathbf{x}-\mathbf{S}^{\dagger}\mathbf{S}\mathbf{x}\|_{2}^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math> The results show that the QR-initialized matrix provides good invertibility across all datasets, and that optimizing <math id="A1.SS12.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐒</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{S}</annotation></semantics></math> via Eq. (<a href="#S3.E3" title="In 3.2 Learning the NPN Prior ‣ 3 Method ‣ NPN: Non-Linear Projections of the Null-Space for Imaging Inverse Problems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>) on each dataset further improves it. Thus, the data distribution can enhance the data-driven invertibility of an already orthogonal matrix. Testing <math id="A1.SS12.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐒</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{S}</annotation></semantics></math> on in-distribution samples yields the <span id="A1.SS12.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_bold">best</span> invertibility (<span id="A1.SS12.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_bold">bold</span>), while diverse training data (e.g. CIFAR10) gives the second-best (underlined), suggesting a single <math id="A1.SS12.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐒</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{S}</annotation></semantics></math> could generalize across datasets.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.T9" class="ltx_table">
<div id="A1.T9.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:345.0pt;height:49.3pt;vertical-align:-22.7pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-46.1pt,6.6pt) scale(0.789294655035473,0.789294655035473) ;">
<table id="A1.T9.2.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="A1.T9.2.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T9.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_tt">Test/<math id="A1.T9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐒</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{S}</annotation></semantics></math> design</td>
<td id="A1.T9.2.1.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_tt"><math id="A1.T9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{QR}(\mathbf{H})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐇</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{QR}(\mathbf{H})</annotation></semantics></math> Alg <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ A.2 Algorithms for designing 𝐒 ‣ Appendix A Technical Appendices ‣ NPN: Non-Linear Projections of the Null-Space for Imaging Inverse Problems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></td>
<td id="A1.T9.2.1.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_tt"><span id="A1.T9.2.1.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">MNIST</span></td>
<td id="A1.T9.2.1.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_tt"><span id="A1.T9.2.1.1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">FashionMNIST</span></td>
<td id="A1.T9.2.1.1.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_tt"><span id="A1.T9.2.1.1.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">CIFAR10</span></td>
<td id="A1.T9.2.1.1.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt"><span id="A1.T9.2.1.1.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">CelebA</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T9.2.1.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T9.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><span id="A1.T9.2.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">MNIST</span></td>
<td id="A1.T9.2.1.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><math id="A1.T9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="9.28\times 10^{-5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>9.28</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">9.28\times 10^{-5}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A1.T9.2.1.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><math id="A1.T9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{2.97\times 10^{-5}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold">2.97</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>𝟏𝟎</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>𝟓</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{2.97\times 10^{-5}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A1.T9.2.1.2.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><math id="A1.T9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{4.99\times 10^{-5}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mn>4.99</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{4.99\times 10^{-5}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A1.T9.2.1.2.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><math id="A1.T9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5.29\times 10^{-5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>5.29</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5.29\times 10^{-5}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A1.T9.2.1.2.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><math id="A1.T9.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5.56\times 10^{-5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>5.56</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5.56\times 10^{-5}</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T9.2.1.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T9.2.1.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><span id="A1.T9.2.1.3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">FashionMNIST</span></td>
<td id="A1.T9.2.1.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><math id="A1.T9.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.76\times 10^{-4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1.76</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.76\times 10^{-4}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
