<td id="A1.T9.2.1.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><math id="A1.T9.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2.39\times 10^{-4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2.39</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2.39\times 10^{-4}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A1.T9.2.1.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><math id="A1.T9.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.55\times 10^{-4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1.55</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.55\times 10^{-4}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A1.T9.2.1.5.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><math id="A1.T9.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="9.09\times 10^{-5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>9.09</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">9.09\times 10^{-5}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A1.T9.2.1.5.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><math id="A1.T9.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{4.68\times 10^{-5}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mn>4.68</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{4.68\times 10^{-5}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A1.T9.2.1.5.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t"><math id="A1.T9.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{4.15\times 10^{-5}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold">4.15</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>𝟏𝟎</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>𝟓</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{4.15\times 10^{-5}}</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
</table>
</span></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 9: </span>Cross dataset validation of data invertibility metric <math id="A1.T9.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{x}}\|\mathbf{x}-\mathbf{S}^{\dagger}\mathbf{S}\mathbf{x}\|_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐒</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐒𝐱</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{x}}\|\mathbf{x}-\mathbf{S}^{\dagger}\mathbf{S}\mathbf{x}\|_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS13" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.13 </span>Limitations on the selection of <math id="A1.SS13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐒</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{S}</annotation></semantics></math></h3>

<div id="A1.SS13.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS13.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The method works when it is possible to find a non-linear correlation between null space (NS) components <math id="A1.SS13.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Sx}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐒𝐱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Sx}</annotation></semantics></math> and measurements <math id="A1.SS13.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Hx}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐇𝐱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Hx}</annotation></semantics></math>, leveraging a dataset with triplets <math id="A1.SS13.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathbf{x}_{i},\mathbf{Hx}_{i},\mathbf{Sx}_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐇𝐱</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐒𝐱</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathbf{x}_{i},\mathbf{Hx}_{i},\mathbf{Sx}_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>. We promote this correlation by solving Eq. (<a href="#S3.E3" title="In 3.2 Learning the NPN Prior ‣ 3 Method ‣ NPN: Non-Linear Projections of the Null-Space for Imaging Inverse Problems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>) that balances the two terms: i) <math id="A1.SS13.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathbf{Sx}-\mathrm{G}(\mathbf{Hx})\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐒𝐱</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐇𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathbf{Sx}-\mathrm{G}(\mathbf{Hx})\|</annotation></semantics></math> encourages a non-linear correlation between <math id="A1.SS13.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Sx}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐒𝐱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Sx}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS13.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Hx}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐇𝐱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Hx}</annotation></semantics></math>. ii) <math id="A1.SS13.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathbf{I}-\mathbf{A}^{\top}\mathbf{A}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐈</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐀</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathbf{I}-\mathbf{A}^{\top}\mathbf{A}\|</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A1.SS13.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{A}=[\mathbf{H}^{\top},\mathbf{S}^{\top}]^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐇</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐒</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{A}=[\mathbf{H}^{\top},\mathbf{S}^{\top}]^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> promotes orthogonality and ensures that <math id="A1.SS13.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐒</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{S}</annotation></semantics></math> samples components from the NS of <math id="A1.SS13.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐇</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{H}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS13.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS13.p2.1" class="ltx_p">There are scenarios where the non-linear correlations are easier to achieve, for instance, in deblurring or SR, due to the low-pass filters associated with these tasks being non-ideal, which leads to close frequency bands between the high-pass components selected by <math id="A1.SS13.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐒</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{S}</annotation></semantics></math> and the Gaussian-like low-pass components sampled by <math id="A1.SS13.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐇</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{H}</annotation></semantics></math>. In other scenarios, such as MRI or CT, the non-linear correlations between <math id="A1.SS13.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Sx}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐒𝐱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Sx}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS13.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Hx}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐇𝐱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Hx}</annotation></semantics></math> are more challenging to achieve due to the orthogonality of their respective rows. But, the method still works by designing <math id="A1.SS13.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐒</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{S}</annotation></semantics></math> such that it leverages structural similarities of <math id="A1.SS13.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐇</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{H}</annotation></semantics></math>, such as adjacent frequencies in MRI or neighboring angles in CT.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS13.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS13.p3.1" class="ltx_p">To illustrate the effectiveness of finding non-linear correlations between <math id="A1.SS13.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Sx}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐒𝐱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Sx}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS13.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Hx}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐇𝐱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Hx}</annotation></semantics></math>, we set a challenging scenario in an MRI task with <math id="A1.SS13.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐇</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{H}</annotation></semantics></math> sampling only random low frequencies using a 1D Cartesian mask with an acceleration factor (AF) of 12. We then apply an FFTSHIFT operation to this mask to produce a high-frequency sampling pattern, denoted by <math id="A1.SS13.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{S}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐒</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{S}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, spatially distant from the frequency support of <math id="A1.SS13.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐇</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{H}</annotation></semantics></math> but maintaining the same AF. We refer to this configuration as the well-separated sampling. In this case, the method fails to recover non-trivial solutions, <math id="A1.SS13.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathrm{G}^{*}(\mathbf{y})\|=0.0108" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>G</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.0108</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathrm{G}^{*}(\mathbf{y})\|=0.0108</annotation></semantics></math>, and a high relative error of <math id="A1.SS13.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1.0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS13.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS13.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Then, we configure a scenario where the non-linear correlations are easier to find, using the same <math id="A1.SS13.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐇</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{H}</annotation></semantics></math> described before, we set <math id="A1.SS13.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{S}_{2}=\mathbf{I}-\mathbf{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐒</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝐈</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐇</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{S}_{2}=\mathbf{I}-\mathbf{H}</annotation></semantics></math> that selects frequencies adjacent to those sampled by <math id="A1.SS13.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐇</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{H}</annotation></semantics></math>. This adjacent sampling configuration corresponds precisely to the setup employed in the MRI experiments presented in the main manuscript. See Figure <a href="#A1.F10" title="Figure 10 ‣ A.13 Limitations on the selection of 𝐒 ‣ Appendix A Technical Appendices ‣ NPN: Non-Linear Projections of the Null-Space for Imaging Inverse Problems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>. It exhibits increased spectral (non-linear) correlation, resulting in a small relative error of 0.325, and a norm <math id="A1.SS13.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathrm{G}^{*}(\mathbf{y})\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>G</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathrm{G}^{*}(\mathbf{y})\|</annotation></semantics></math> close to the norm of the ground-truth signal <math id="A1.SS13.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathbf{Sx}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐒𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathbf{Sx}\|</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.F10" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.01608v1/nonlinear.png" id="A1.F10.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:429/153;" width="429" height="153" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 10: </span>MRI masks</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A1.T10" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 10: </span>Comparison of reconstruction metrics under different sampling strategies.</figcaption>
<table id="A1.T10.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="A1.T10.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T10.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t"><span id="A1.T10.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Sampling Type</span></td>
<td id="A1.T10.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><math id="A1.T10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dfrac{\|\mathbf{Sx}^{\*}-\mathrm{G}^{\*}(\mathbf{y})\|}{\|\mathbf{Sx}^{\*}\|}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐒𝐱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msup><mi>𝐒𝐱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dfrac{\|\mathbf{Sx}^{\*}-\mathrm{G}^{\*}(\mathbf{y})\|}{\|\mathbf{Sx}^{\*}\|}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A1.T10.2.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><math id="A1.T10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathrm{G}^{\*}(\mathbf{y})\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathrm{G}^{\*}(\mathbf{y})\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A1.T10.2.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><math id="A1.T10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathbf{Sx}^{\*}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msup><mi>𝐒𝐱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathbf{Sx}^{\*}\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A1.T10.2.1.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">PSNR(<math id="A1.T10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{G}^{\*}(\mathbf{y}),\mathbf{Sx}^{\*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐒𝐱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{G}^{\*}(\mathbf{y}),\mathbf{Sx}^{\*}</annotation></semantics></math>) [dB]</td></tr>
